```java
class Branch {
    private final List<Vehicle> fleet;
    private final Map<String, IntervalSet> bookedRanges; // vehicleId -> booked date ranges

    Reservation reserve(VehicleCategory category, DateRange range) {
        for (Vehicle v : fleet) {
            if (v.getCategory() == category && !bookedRanges.get(v.getId()).overlaps(range)) {
                bookedRanges.get(v.getId()).add(range);
                return new Reservation(v.getCategory(), range, v.getId());
            }
        }
        throw new NoAvailabilityException(category, range);
    }
}
```

`reserve` still just needs *one* matching vehicle with no overlapping booking — the interesting
part isn't this loop, it's how `overlaps(range)` avoids being a per-day scan, which the next two
slides cover.
